$-\mathrm{NO}_2$ is electron withdrawing group and therefore decreases the electron density on the carbanion and thus stabilises the conjugate base. $-\mathrm{NH}_2$ is electron donating group and therefore increases the electron density on the carbanion and thus destabilises the conjugate base. Therefore, the acidity order is II > I > III.

